---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Prose
  title="Privacy"
  standfirst="What little data I hold, why, and for how long."
  updated="TBD"
>
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="tbd">{site.tradingName}</span>, contactable at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, is the data controller
    for this site.
  </p>

  <h2>This site sets no cookies</h2>
  <p>
    There is no analytics, no advertising, and no tracking on these pages. That
    is why there is no cookie banner. Stripe's checkout, which opens when you
    buy, sets its own cookies for payment and fraud prevention.
  </p>

  <h2>What I collect when you order</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, email address and delivery address</li>
    <li>The colours you chose</li>
    <li>What you ordered and what you paid</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    I need these to make the thing, post it to you, and keep proper records. The
    legal basis is performance of our contract, and legal obligation for the
    records HMRC requires.
  </p>
  <p>
    I never see your card details. Stripe processes payments and holds that data
    as its own controller — see
    <a href="https://stripe.com/gb/privacy" rel="noopener">Stripe's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Stripe — payment processing</li>
    <li>Royal Mail or a similar carrier — the delivery address on the parcel</li>
    <li>My email provider — messages you send me</li>
  </ul>
  <p>I do not sell your data or send marketing you did not ask for.</p>

  <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Order and payment records for six years, as UK tax law requires. Emails for
    as long as they are useful, then deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask me for a copy of your data, to correct it, or to delete it where
    I am not required to keep it. Email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and I will respond within
    a month.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are unhappy with how I have handled your data you can complain to the
    Information Commissioner's Office at
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
  </p>
</Prose>
